</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44e5f5c-adbe-11f1-9c3c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253314185952.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44e5f5c-adbe-11f1-9c3c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253314185952.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e06e5590-ad6b-11f1-b0c8-3522566f6c27</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 04:52:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b44e5f5c-adbe-11f1-9c3c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253314185952.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels seize strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-yemen-houthis-city-red-sea-iran</link><description>
Yemen’s Houthis seized the strategic Red Sea port city of Mocha on Thursday as their offensive against Saudi-backed government forces intensified. Saudi Arabia launched dozens of airstrikes over the past 24 hours, the Houthis said, after the Iran-backed group carried out attacks on Saudi territory that wounded dozens of people.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e558ca48-ad68-11f1-8a2a-3522566f6c27</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:55:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6446b3f2-abb0-11f1-b7c5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/c11f1b5f361174a659ad76cf10d47f1376a66e00.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel destroys Hezbollah tunnel network in south Lebanon, triggering 4.1-magnitude tremor</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israel-hezbollah-tunnels-lebanon-earthquake</link><description>
