</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07cce53a-ad61-11f1-97b3-23806945c836</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 21:50:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33fe30ea-ad7b-11f1-9da7-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AFP-20260910-C7Y769E-v3-MidRes-TopshotLebanonIsraelIranUsWar.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran-backed Houthi rebels take strategic port city in Yemen, raising threat to Red Sea shipping</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/iran-backed-houthi-rebels-take-strategic-port-city-in-yemen-raising-threat-to-red-sea-shipping</link><description>
The Iran-backed Houthi rebel group on Thursday took over Yemen’s port city of Mokha, an area vital to controlling shipping through the Red Sea, Houthi and Yemeni officials said. Mokha is about 80 kilometers (50 miles) from the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a waterway that connects the Red Sea and the Gulf of Aden and through which about 12% of the world’s goods are typically shipped. FRANCE 24's Nick Rushworth reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f4ef6c-ad46-11f1-9715-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-15T154107Z-1357356968-RC23ZMARBWJD-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-SAUDI-MOCHA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/68f4ef6c-ad46-11f1-9715-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-15T154107Z-1357356968-RC23ZMARBWJD-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-SAUDI-MOCHA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be3f3022-ad4b-11f1-af36-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:18:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran raises fuel prices for heavy users</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/iran-raises-fuel-prices-for-heavy-users</link><description>
The rise of the price of fuel is an issue for both the United States and Iran in this conflict. US president Donald Trump has conceded that prices will not fall before the midterm elections where the US voters could hold him to account. Meanwhile in Iran where many communities have been bombed since February 28th, there's now the added problem of incresing fuel prices. FRANCE 24's Ali al Basha sent this report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7ccf6e-ad48-11f1-974d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8930421296aa2fb36042431-60179231.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c7ccf6e-ad48-11f1-974d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-8930421296aa2fb36042431-60179231.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9a0ed56-ad46-11f1-941f-39e6bfb413de</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:48:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli-made film about use of AI for mass killing in Gaza gets record ovation at Venice premiere</title><link>http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260910-israeli-made-film-about-mass-killings-in-gaza-gets-25-minute-ovation-at-venice-premiere</link><description>
A film documenting Israel's use of artificial intelligence to facilitate the mass killing of Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip received a record 25-minute standing ovation at the Venice Film Festival on Thursday. "NAZA" details the brutal Israeli bombardment of the Palestinian territory through anonymous interviews with two dozen whistleblowers from the Israeli military or intelligence services.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/160943d0-ad22-11f1-83ed-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/6313157432cdcb86dbc5df006a22ed29851403a3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/160943d0-ad22-11f1-83ed-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/6313157432cdcb86dbc5df006a22ed29851403a3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">202c9408-ad44-11f1-869d-c5efca00c8f8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:19:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/160943d0-ad22-11f1-83ed-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/6313157432cdcb86dbc5df006a22ed29851403a3.jpg">© Stefano Rellandini, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
